  "content": {
    "_uid": "bf74becb-2c42-3520-521c-06c4eeb20228",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "08221594-02f0-e802-5f9e-ad2e5c182a8d",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Thus, a simulation-based course was designed and offered to the AKUH secondary hospitals (Garden, Karimabad, Kharadar and Hyderabad) to improve the competency of their staff in the domain of maternal and child health. The participants attended a theoretical session and practical demonstrations via Zoom a day prior to the simulation. They gathered at CIME the next day for hands-on practice sessions right after a quick review of the concepts that had been discussed online. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "This extensive course provided participants with lots of hands-on experience of the surgical skills required for effectively managing maternal collapse. These trained individuals are now confident that they can more effectively manage these catastrophic complications in any setting.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
