    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Maternal mortality is one of the major concerns of low and middle income countries as these countries share a large percentage of maternal deaths which are mostly from preventable causes. Competent health care providers are an invaluable asset in the battle to reduce the number of maternal deaths. These front line healthcare providers can identify the alarming signs, perform risk stratification and then initiate management in a timely manner or refer patient to tertiary care hospitals. By optimizing each of these steps, we can help improve both maternal and neonatal outcomes. The healthcare team, which includes midwives, nurses, and doctors, should be well-equipped with the skills to deal with unprecedented circumstances and medical complications to ensure the safety of their patients.",
